Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 22:11:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02201/11362] [outer-loop] WIRE the ARC learning loop into a
 standing entrypoint (conductor-runnable)

scripts/arc_loop_solve.py --game <X>: routing -> verifier-routed solve -> reproduction
gate -> train+checkpoint learned verifier -> registry. Self-improves across runs
(loads the saved learned verifier next time). arc_game_adapters.py = per-game adapter
registry (lp85 reference). Validated: lp85->L3 reproduced, 359-state search, checkpoint
written; tn36->routing recommendation (delta-RE starting point). CLAUDE.md discipline
now points the ARC north-star task at this entrypoint, so the planner emits ARC tasks
that run the standing loop. Did NOT touch research_conductor.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
